WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.538
This specification
took forty-five

00:02.538 --> 00:04.000
minutes to produce.

00:06.000 --> 00:07.659
You give it one
goal — or a meeting

00:07.659 --> 00:09.610
transcript — and it
runs a full interview

00:09.610 --> 00:10.610
for you.

00:13.000 --> 00:15.125
One question per
turn. Every answer

00:15.125 --> 00:17.000
logged, every
category tracked.

00:19.000 --> 00:23.000
Seven stages. Each
one gates the next.

00:23.000 --> 00:24.875
The specification
maps roles to

00:24.875 --> 00:27.000
actions, permissions
and workflows.

00:28.000 --> 00:30.267
Processes become
diagrams. Diagrams

00:30.267 --> 00:32.000
get reviewed
before export.

00:34.500 --> 00:35.891
One spec, three
formats — HTML to

00:35.891 --> 00:37.413
read, PDF to sign or
print, Markdown

00:37.413 --> 00:38.500
for your
AI coding agents.

00:42.500 --> 00:44.273
Reopen any finished
session, confirm the

00:44.273 --> 00:46.091
open items, and the
specification updates

00:46.091 --> 00:47.091
in place.

00:49.000 --> 00:51.600
MIT licensed. Try the
demo replay in the

00:51.600 --> 00:53.000
browser — no install.
